{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-13T09:25:00.844Z",
  "steps": [
    "In an empty project the new recipe entry opens guidance, offers no invented actor, disables Create, and writes no author data.",
    "The ordinary World GUI creates an OC and then a compatible RPG player projection with size 72×88, speed 180 and blue color. Its source relationship points to that OC; no fixture author objects are injected.",
    "Three rows mix two references to the same projection and one ordinary OC. Removing one row preserves both surviving UUIDs and placement identity; replacement receives a fresh UUID. An unfinished minus coordinate survives native select row changes and cannot be reviewed. Editing invalidates review. Chinese, English and Japanese at 390px preserve every row and reviewed JSON; header/footer stay reachable. Cancel changes neither author data nor editor state.",
    "Create transfers all three reviewed rows to one ordinary unsaved JSON draft; ordinary Save persists the exact bytes and one registration. Both projection actors remain symbolic inheritance declarations, while the plain OC retains explicit baseline fields. Earlier OC/projection bytes stay unchanged.",
    "Saved preview resolves both references independently to the same inherited 72×88, blue, speed-180 projection. Materialization preserves all three UUIDs, author order and individual coordinates, keeping inherited fields unflattened. It creates only an independent Scene2D and its registration.",
    "Real Godot plan/build/headless execution succeeds with three distinct scene identities. The two projection instances each move 45px and the plain actor moves 40px under the shared arrow-input step, preserving their different starting coordinates. Plan/build/run change no author bytes. This checks repeated definitions and distinct runtime instances, not independently routed control bindings."
  ],
